  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 131 PM CDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nLate Tuesday our resident upper ridge gets better established again \nwith the center over E/SE TX. While deep monsoonal flow works over \nthe western periphery, abundant storm activity over Far W TX and NM \nwill only enhance the inflow low level winds and enhance onshore \nwinds. So while the ridge keeps the weather hot, the winds keep the \nRH values elevated for high heat indices topping 100 each day \nthrough mid week. A few showers and storms could get going in the \nafternoons, but the ridging overhead should keep the coverage closer \nto around 10 percent after Tuesday. The ridge continues to amplify \nlate in the week which should lead to reduced onshore flow and a \ndrier and more stable regime heading into the weekend. This will \nhopefully lower morning low temperatures and afternoon heat index \nvalues, but offer no relief from the ambient high temperatures.",
